    "summary": "This Reaction allows the Reacting Unit to split into two new Units when an enemy Unit ends its move within 12\".",
    "description": "**Trigger:** Once per Battle, the Reactive Player may declare a The Blade Splits Advanced Reaction in Step 2 of the Move Sub-Phase process, if an enemy Unit ends a move within 12\" and Line of Sight of a Unit under the Reactive Player's Control.\n\n**Cost:** The Reactive Player must spend 1 point of their Reaction Allotment to declare a The Blade Splits Advanced Reaction, this cost paid as soon as the declaration is made.\n\n**Target:** The Target Unit is always the Unit whose Move triggered the Advanced Reaction. Once the cost has been paid, the Reactive Player must select one Unit under their control that is within 12\" and has Line of Sight to the Target Unit, and which contains only Models with the Legio Custodes and The Sodality Traits, and which also contains at least six Models. That Unit is the Reacting Unit.\n\n**Process:** 1. Once the The Blade Spits Advanced Reaction has been declared, the Active Player must completely resolve the Target Unit's Movement.\n2. Once the Target Unit has finished its move, the Reactive Player must move a number of Models from the Reacting Unit. When making this move, the Reactive Player must move at least three Models from the Reacting Unit a number of inches up to the Base Value of each Model's Initiative Characteristic so that they are no longer in Unit Coherency with the rest of the Reacting Unit, but are in Unit Coherency with each other. Once this movement is complete, there must still be at least three Models from the Reacting Unit which did not move and which are still in Unit Coherency with each other.\n3. Once this movement has been resolved, the Models from the Reacting Unit which moved are considered to form a new Unit separate from the rest of the Reacting Unit for all purposes, including the scoring of Victory Points (excluding the Last Man Standing (X) Secondary Objective). All Models which were in the Reacting Unit when The Blade Splits Advanced Reaction was declared are considered to have made a Reaction in this Player Turn.",
